w  i've undergone a lot of training i've  you know been to through a lot of school  i've you know faced a lot of challenges  and i'm still standing i'm still here i  find a way to get through all of it and  you didn't get through all of these  gates by accident nobody accidentally  let you into college and you didn't  accidentally graduate and you  accidentally get to grad school and you  accidentally get a job like who has that  kind of luck right um so  at a certain point you really need to  start to believe that you're not here by  a you know a clerical error uh you  earned your spot and then recall all the  things that previously seemed impossible  that you managed to do  uh and start to you know own who you are  i still have self-doubt i still get  nerves um or you get you see this  daunting task in front of you um and  also for that my family and you know my  peers that i went through grad school  with we hype each other up and we're not  hyping each other up with lies we i feel  like it's so much easier for someone  external to you to see your greatness so  if my friend calls me from grad school  and it's like i don't know how i'm gonna  do this oh my girl are you kidding me do  you remember that you did this and this  and this and he didn't even help you and  you did this and this so it's so easy to  see the greatness in someone else so let  your friends and your support network  and your family  show a mirror hold a mirror up to you  and show you your greatness and hype you  up because you've done a lot and you  will do so much more  thank you for that i know that answer  probably helped a lot of people um who  struggle with imposter syndrome so thank  you  um there's another question here from  one of the attendees and i am not a  scientist so i'm just going to read it  and let you  answer as you will but  the question is what is your opinion on  single atom catalyst  do you think that it's possible to  replace nanoparticle catalyst in the  future  so i'm 